### Fleet Provisioning (REAL production) ####
👉 Devices generate certs by themselves

Flow:
Device gets a bootstrap (claim) certificate
Device connects to AWS IoT
Calls provisioning API
AWS:
Creates Thing
Generates certificate
Attaches policy
Device stores new cert and uses it permanently
--------------------------------------------

![alt text](Fleetprovision.png)

🔹 Step 1: Create a Claim Certificate
One shared certificate for all devices (temporary)
🔹 Step 2: Embed claim cert in device firmware

👉 Same cert for all devices (easy to deploy)

🔹 Step 3: Device connects to AWS IoT
Using:
Claim certificate
🔹 Step 4: Device requests provisioning
Sends:
Device ID (serial number / MAC)

🔹 Step 5: AWS creates:
Thing
Unique certificate
Policy

🔹 Step 6: Device stores new cert locally

👉 Now becomes permanent identity

🔹 Step 7: Device reconnects using new cert

👉 Now fully secure MQTT

## ---------------------------------------

Migration HTTPs to MQTT

You can do hybrid migration:

Phase 1:
Device calls your API
API returns: Claim cert OR provisioning trigger

Phase 2:
Device switches to MQTT

👍 What you need to implement
✅ On AWS side:
Provisioning template
Claim certificate
IoT policy
✅ On device side:
Store:
Claim cert (temporary)
After provisioning:
Store permanent cert

